    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d522">

                <pb facs="0655" n="341" xml:id="pg341"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/514½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring
                        Rice</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Counselor for the
                            Department of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-09">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 11</hi>.] </dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Counsellor</hi>: I duly received the
                    official letter from your Department dated November 7 relative to the protest of
                    your Government on the subject of the detention of United States vessels in
                    British ports and other matters.</p>
                <p>I lost no time in telegraphing its contents to my Government and I will send a
                    copy by the next mail. In the meanwhile I have received telegrams from my
                    Government, copies of which I enclose for you herewith, which provide
                    information as to the arrangements now being made with neutral governments with
                    the object of putting as few hindrances as possible in the way of neutral trade
                    and shipping, while carrying out those measures of restriction which present
                    hostilities have unfortunately made necessary.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>





